## Tool Selection Decision Tree

### User wants to work with code
- Read/write/create C# scripts → **manage_script**
- Read/write non-C# files (JSON, YAML, txt, shader, etc.) → **manage_file**
- Find symbol definitions, usages, file structure → **search_code** (requires indexing)
- Evaluate a C# expression at runtime → **execute_code** (restricted, must activate)

### User wants to operate on scene objects
- Find objects by name/tag/layer/component → **find_gameobjects**
- Create/delete/modify/reparent GameObjects → **manage_gameobject**
- Add/remove/configure components → **manage_component**
- Scene-level ops (open/save/list/hierarchy) → **manage_scene**
- Read-only analysis (health, stats, hotspots) → **scene_analysis**

### User wants to work with assets
- Search/create/delete/move asset files → **manage_asset**
- Prefab create/instantiate/apply/unpack → **manage_prefab** (activate Scripting)
- ScriptableObject CRUD → **manage_scriptable_object** (activate Scripting)
- Material create/modify/batch → **manage_material** (activate Material)
- **Shader create/modify** → **manage_shader** (activate Shader)
- **Animation clip / AnimatorController / state machine** → **manage_animation** (activate Animation)
- Import settings for textures/models/generic → **manage_texture_import / manage_model_import / manage_asset_import** (activate Utility)

### User wants UI work
- Legacy uGUI (Canvas/Button/Text/Image) → **manage_ui** (activate Specialized)
- UI Toolkit (UXML/USS/UIDocument) → **manage_ui_toolkit** (activate Specialized)

### User wants diagnostics/optimization
- Console errors/warnings/system info → **read_console**
- Scene performance analysis → **scene_analysis** action:find_hotspots / performance_hints
- Profiler data → **manage_profiler** (activate Extended)
- **Compilation status / recompile / wait for compile / list assemblies** → **manage_compilation** (activate Meta; get_status/get_last_errors/request_compilation/wait_for_compilation/get_assemblies)
- Batch optimization (textures/meshes/audio) → **optimization** (activate Extended)
- Missing references/unused assets/duplicates → **cleaner** (activate Extended)
- **Memory snapshot / memory leak / .snap file / heap analysis** → **manage_memory_profiler** (activate Extended; take_memory_snapshot/list/analyze/diff — take+list need no external package)
- **Scene physics stats / layer collision matrix / raycast(2D) / overlap(capsule)** → **manage_physics** (activate Specialized; list_scene_physics_stats / get_collision_matrix / raycast dimension=2d / overlap_test shape=capsule)

### User wants project-level operations
- Build settings/trigger build → **manage_build** (activate Extended)
- Package install/remove/list → **manage_package** (activate Extended)
- Run tests → **manage_test** (activate Extended)
- Tags/layers management → **manage_tags_layers** (activate Extended)
- Editor state/play mode/selection → **manage_editor** (rich selection via set_selection_by_query + mode=add/remove)
- **EditorPrefs / PlayerPrefs (per-user editor or app state)** → **manage_prefs** (activate Meta; has/get/set/delete/delete_all — **destructive**, non-undoable)
- **SceneView pivot/size/rotation** → **manage_camera** (activate Specialized; get_scene_view / set_scene_view)
- **NavMesh bake / query / clear** → **manage_navmesh** (activate Extended)
- **Smart batch operations (batch-rename / find-replace across scene / cross-cutting refactors)** → **smart_operations** (activate Extended)
- **Execute any Unity Editor menu item by path (e.g., "Assets/Create/Material", "Window/Analysis/Profiler")** → **execute_menu_item** (activate Meta)
- **Git / SVN / Perforce operations (status / diff / commit / pull / log / branches)** — when user says "提交" / "commit" / "看修改" / "推送" / "pull the changes" → **version_control** (activate VersionControl)
- Repetitive bulk operations → **workflow**

### User wants to store/retrieve knowledge
- Long-term cross-session memories → **manage_memory** (activate Cloud)
- Project knowledge base (RAG) → **manage_knowledge** (activate Cloud)
- Workspace config (PROJECT.md / SOUL.ext.md) → **manage_workspace_config**

### User wants to SEE a view / verify visual execution (Vision Model)
- **vision_analyze** (activate Meta; action=capture → PNG files; action=analyze → PNG + Vision Model text description) — USE FOR:
  - User asks to "see the view" / "check the game screen" / "verify how it looks" / "看画面 / 看效果 / 看 UI 对不对 / 看我执行的视觉结果"
  - You just performed a **visual** change (UI layout, material colors, scene arrangement, prefab placement, rendering) and want to self-confirm the result before claiming done.
  - Debugging visual-only issues (clipping, misalignment, color, object not visible) that code inspection cannot confirm.
- **Choose `source` by intent (don't just use auto blindly)**:
  - `game` — the **real running render** (main camera). Use for: verifying actual rendering/runtime effect (post-processing, particles, runtime UI), matching what the player sees.
  - `scene` — the **user's current SceneView view** (camera follows what the user is looking at). Use for: aligning with what the user describes/discusses ("look at this wall"), user's current framing/layout, edit-time arrangement. Output is a **clean geometry render** (no grid/gizmo/selection overlay).
  - `game_and_scene` — both, for **comparing** effect (e.g. user frames position A in scene but the game renders position B → spot the discrepancy).
  - `auto` (default) — PlayMode→`game`, Edit→`scene`.
- **Result metadata (no visual guessing)**: every result returns `view=` (camera position / pivot / rotation) and `selection=` (current selection's instanceId/name/path/position from the Selection API). Use these to correlate the image with what the user is looking at / has selected — **never guess what is selected or where from the pixels**; read the returned metadata.
- **Two-stage / region zoom (`region` param) — USE FOR seeing far / small / occluded detail**: whole-view screenshots downscale fine detail, so the model often misses small or distant objects. When you need a closer look, do a two-stage call:
  1. `action=analyze` (no region) → overview + identify a suspicious area ("left-center, small dark box near the base").
  2. `action=analyze region="x,y,w,h"` with normalized viewport coords (0-1, **bottom-left origin**) → returns the cropped PNG for that area, so the model sees raw pixels instead of a downscaled whole view. Example: `region="0.3,0.4,0.2,0.2"` zooms into the left-lower area. This is **optional**: omit it for a normal whole-view analyze. Region is applied to the same rendered frame (crop of the full image), not a camera re-frame, and the output filename carries `_crop_<x>_<y>_<w>_<h>`.
- **⚠ Activation**: `vision_analyze` is OnDemand — even though it appears in "Available Tools", it is NOT in your active tool schema until you call `request_tools action:activate categories:["Meta"]`. If a call returns "not available / not found", activate it first, then retry.
- **⚠ Vision Model not configured**: `action=analyze` fails with a config hint when the Vision Model is not enabled/configured (Project Settings > AgentCore > Model & Agent → Vision Model card). **Do NOT retry blindly** — instead:
  1. Tell the user Vision Model is not configured and where to enable it (endpoint/model/apiKey).
  2. `action=capture` works **without** a vision model (pure PNG); or use `manage_camera:render_to_texture` / `execute_code` to save the image, then report the file path to the user.
  3. Only retry analyze after the user confirms they configured it.

